CORE
main.c
-D_GNU_SOURCE
^EXIT=(0|10)$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION (SUCCESSFUL|FAILED)$
--
^warning: ignoring
map::at
--
A library model may call a function that is only declared in the library, for
example because a system header renames it via an asm label, and that has no
model either. Calling it must not abort symbolic execution, which used to fail
with "map::at" as the function had no entry in the goto functions. Whether the
callee has a model depends on the platform's C library, hence the result is not
checked.
